---
import Layout from '../layouts/MinimalLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';

import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';

import '../styles/home.css';
import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="NYC Physics Tutor">
	<Hero 
		name={SITE_DATA.name} 
		tagline="Physics Tutoring with 20+ Years of Experience" 
		twitter={SITE_DATA.twitter}
		linkedin={SITE_DATA.linkedin}
		scholar={SITE_DATA.scholar}
		email={SITE_DATA.email}
	/>

    <div class="page-container">
        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-intro-wrapper centered-column">
                <p class="intro-text">
                    Since 2003, I've provided expert one-on-one instruction for high school and university students across New York City. You will benefit from my deep familiarity with local curricula, access to targeted problem sets, and a patient approach that is entirely tailored to how you or your student learns.
                <br><br>
                    Call or text me at <a href="tel:+17187537060">718-753-7060</a>, email me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>cjhellwig@gmail.com</a>, or use the <a href="#contact">contact form</a> below. Let’s map out a plan for upcoming tests and coursework. Reach out today to discuss goals and schedule a session. 
                </p>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>Proven Experience in NYC’s Top Schools</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
					I’ve been tutoring physics and math in New York City for over two decades. Because I work extensively with students from top local independent and prep schools—including Trinity, Dalton, Chapin, and Horace Mann—as well as with undergraduates and post-bacs at NYU and Columbia, I know the exact pacing, rigor, and expectations of your physics syllabus.
					<br><br>
					Whether we are dealing with a high school intro course, AP Physics C E&M, or college-level physics pre-med requirements, I already know the exact demands of these courses, having guided dozens of students through them successfully.
				</p>
			</section>

            <section>
                <h2>The Approach: Experience, Patience, and Vast Resources</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
					I’ve explained these concepts hundreds of times to students across a wide spectrum of backgrounds and learning styles. However, tutoring isn't just about me simply lecturing or explaining concepts; most of our time is spent working through problems together. I'm able to give students enough hints and clues so they can work through the problems with effort but without frustration or time-wasting detours, because that is where real learning happens. Beyond a patient guide, students gain access to a massive archive of curated practice problems, past exams, and custom flashcard decks. The best way to do well on a test is to work through similar problems, and I have both the resources and the discernment to provide students with the exact practice they'll need to walk into test day fully prepared.
				</p>
			</section>

            <section>
                <h2>Subjects Covered</h2>
                <ul class="education-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">High School</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">From Honors Physics and advanced tracks to AP Physics 1, 2, and C (Mechanics & E&M), I help students at elite NYC independent and prep schools like Trinity, Dalton, Horace Mann, and Chapin master the coursework, and I have a strong, proven track record of helping them secure a 5 on the exam.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">College & University</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">For undergraduates and post-bacs tackling first-year General Physics I and II—whether algebra or calculus-based—I specialize in helping pre-med students at NYU, Columbia, and other institutions master their foundational science requirements, protect their GPA, and stay on target for medical school and related competitive paths.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
				<h2>Testimonials</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">"Two months before the AP Physics 1 exam, my son Nate thought he was fine self-studying with a chatbot. Then he took a practice test, bombed it, and completely panicked. A family friend told me to call C.J. They spent eight straight weeks on Zoom together, doing intense sessions late into the night. Nate went from completely lost to getting a 5 on the exam. If your kid is in over their head, just hire C.J."
					<br>– David Z.
				</p>
				<p class="intro-text">"C.J. helped me understand concepts in just minutes from Professor Shaevitz' Physics I Course at Columbia University that I would otherwise never have understood. Even though he started tutoring me in the middle of the semester, meeting with C.J. improved my grade significantly, and I actually retained the material as opposed to forgetting it once the course ended. For anyone struggling with physics or any other subjects, definitely contact C.J.!"
					<br>– Marielle Johnson
				</p>
			</section>

            <section id="contact">
                <h2>Ready to Master Physics and Raise Your Grades?</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
                    Call or text me at <a href="tel:+17187537060">718-753-7060</a>, email me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>cjhellwig@gmail.com</a>, or use the contact form below. Let’s map out a plan for your upcoming tests and coursework. Reach out today to discuss your goals and schedule a session. 
				</p>
				<div class="contact-form-section">
		            <ContactForm source="Physics Landing Page"/>
        		</div>
			</section>


        </div>
	</div>
</Layout>
